.\" Manpage for scale-mcp-server.
.TH SCALE-MCP-SERVER 1 "2026-07-27" "scale-mcp-server" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scale-mcp-server \- Model Context Protocol server for IBM Storage Scale
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scale-mcp-server
.RB [ \-\-transport
.IR stdio | http ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-log-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-filesystem-paths
.IR PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scale-mcp-server
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that exposes the IBM Storage Scale
6.0.1 native REST API (\fB/scalemgmt/v3\fR) as MCP tools, alongside v2 GUI
health-monitoring tools and SSH-based CLI tools. MCP clients (such as large
language model agents) connect to the server and invoke these tools to manage
filesystems, filesets, snapshots, quotas, NSDs, nodes, and related resources
on an IBM Storage Scale cluster.
.PP
The server communicates with the cluster over the connection settings
resolved from
.B config/scale_config.ini
and the
.B SCALE_API_*
environment variables (see
.B ENVIRONMENT
and
.BR FILES ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-transport " " { stdio | http }
Transport used to serve MCP clients.
.B http
serves StreamableHTTP;
.B stdio
serves over standard input/output (for clients that launch the server as a
subprocess). Default:
.BR http .
.TP
.BI \-\-host " " ADDRESS
Host address to bind to for the
.B http
transport. Use
.B 0.0.0.0
to bind to all interfaces. Ignored for
.B stdio
transport. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " " PORT
Port number for the
.B http
transport. Ignored for
.B stdio
transport. Default:
.BR 8000 .
.TP
.BI \-\-log-level " " LEVEL
Logging verbosity. One of
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.BR WARNING ,
.BR ERROR ,
or
.BR CRITICAL .
Default:
.BR INFO .
.TP
.BI \-\-filesystem-paths " " "PATH ..."
One or more space-separated directory paths to expose through the optional
file-operations tools. When provided, the server mounts the MCP filesystem
server (launched via
.BR npx )
restricted to these paths. Requires Node.js and
.BR npx .
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every connection setting can be supplied, or overridden, by an environment
variable. When these are set, the configuration file is optional for the REST
API tools.
.TP
.B SCALE_API_HOSTNAME
Cluster hostname (overrides \fBscale_api.hostname\fR).
.TP
.BR SCALE_API_V2_PORT ", " SCALE_API_V3_PORT
GUI (v2) and native REST (v3) API ports.
.TP
.B SCALE_API_TIMEOUT
Request timeout in seconds.
.TP
.BR SCALE_API_USERNAME ", " SCALE_API_PASSWORD
Basic-auth credentials for the REST API.
.TP
.B SCALE_API_ALLOW_INSECURE
When true, disables TLS certificate verification (for self-signed cluster
certificates).
.TP
.BR SCALE_API_CLIENT_CERT ", " SCALE_API_CLIENT_KEY
Paths to a PEM client certificate and key for mTLS authentication. When a
client certificate is configured and no password is set, no basic-auth header
is sent.
.TP
.B SCALE_API_CA_CERT
Path to a CA bundle used to verify the server certificate instead of the
system trust store.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config/scale_config.ini
Cluster connection settings
.RB ( [scale_api] ,
.BR [authorization] ,
.BR [domain] )
and SSH settings
.RB ( [ssh] )
for the CLI tools. Copied from
.BR config/scale_config.ini.example .
Values here are overridden by the
.B SCALE_API_*
environment variables.
.TP
.B config/mcp_config.ini
MCP server settings, including logging configuration. Required at startup;
the server exits with an error if it is missing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns
.B 0
on a clean shutdown. Returns a non-zero status on a usage error (for example,
an invalid option or a missing
.BR config/mcp_config.ini ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with HTTP transport on the default port (localhost only):
.PP
.RS 4
.B scale-mcp-server --transport http
.RE
.PP
Bind the HTTP transport to all interfaces:
.PP
.RS 4
.B scale-mcp-server --transport http --host 0.0.0.0
.RE
.PP
Serve over stdio (for a client that launches the server as a subprocess):
.PP
.RS 4
.B scale-mcp-server --transport stdio
.RE
.PP
Enable the file-operations tools for specific directories:
.PP
.RS 4
.B scale-mcp-server --transport http --filesystem-paths /data /home/user/projects
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation and the IBM Storage Scale native REST API reference:
.PP
.RS 4
https://github.com/IBM/ibm-storage-scale-mcp-server
.br
https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/storage-scale/6.0.1?topic=reference-storage-scale-native-rest-api-endpoints
.RE
